.TH WG-VPN 1 "October 2026" "NetworkManager WireGuard Guard" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
wg-vpn \- manage protected full and split WireGuard tunnels
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B wg-vpn
{homeLAN|workLAB} {full|split|stop|check}
.br
.B wg-vpn
{status|gui|--help|--version}
.SH DESCRIPTION
For full tunnel mode, install an nftables output guard before NetworkManager activates the interface.
Split tunnel mode retains ordinary Internet access via the physical network.
The guest-network indicator represents direct Internet routing permission, not physical packet counts.
.SH CONFIGURATION
/etc/networkmanager-wireguard-guard/sites.json is an administrator-maintained configuration file.
Never publish operational endpoints, keys, addresses, or backups.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B full
Pre-arm the guard and activate the selected full-tunnel profile.
.TP
.B split
Activate the selected split-tunnel profile.
.TP
.B stop
Intentionally disconnect the managed full tunnel and release the guard.
.TP
.B check
Read-only verification of profile and firewall prerequisites.
.TP
.B status
Display connection and guard status.
.TP
.B gui
Open the XFCE two-LED dashboard.
.SH SECURITY
Never activate a full-tunnel connection directly in NetworkManager's menu.
Physical LAN traffic, DHCP and encrypted WireGuard transport may be allowed.
IPv6, roaming and SSH policy require site-specific validation.
.SH RECOVERY
From a local console: sudo wg-guard-reset
